  <div class="inner">
    <div class="mission">
      <p><strong>The Lightning board is finished.</strong> Project Lightning is
      ZeroStick's own 8K controller board — designed in-house, from the traces
      up, and <strong>built exclusively for PC</strong>: native 8,000&nbsp;Hz
      polling, response measured in microseconds, and the drift-resistant TMR
      sticks our controllers are already known for.</p>
      <p>This page is for <strong>businesses that want the board itself</strong> —
      controller brands, modding shops, esports organizations and hardware
      companies who want Lightning in bulk, inside their own products, or on
      their own shelves. Tell us what you're building in the inquiry form
      below.</p>
      <p style="border:.1rem solid rgba(var(--color-foreground),.25);
        border-left:.4rem solid #58a6ff; border-radius:.8rem;
        padding:1.2rem 1.6rem;"><strong>PC only.</strong> Lightning is not a
      console board — it does not connect to a PS5, Xbox or Switch, and it
      never will; consoles cap how fast any controller may report, which
      defeats the entire point of this board. Building for console players?
      The <a href="/pages/zerostick-exo">ZeroStick EXO</a> is the product
      line for that.</p>
      <p>Already have a ZeroStick 8K controller?
      <a href="#app" class="link">Get the free ZS8K Configurator</a> for
      settings and updates.</p>
    </div>

    <h2>Built for exactly one thing</h2>
    <div class="strip">
      <div class="feat"><div class="ico">⚡</div><h3>Native 8K polling</h3>
        <p>8,000 reports a second on PC — not overclocked, not software-forced.
        Native, from the board itself.</p></div>
      <div class="feat"><div class="ico">🎯</div><h3>TMR drift-free sticks</h3>
        <p>The same magnetic TMR stick technology in every ZeroStick build
        today — stable accuracy that doesn't wear into drift.</p></div>
      <div class="feat"><div class="ico">⏱</div><h3>Microsecond response</h3>
        <p>Every part of the signal path chosen for speed. Nothing between
        your thumb and the game that doesn't have to be there.</p></div>
      <div class="feat"><div class="ico">🎮</div><h3>A shell you already know</h3>
        <p>Familiar controller in your hands — Lightning changes what's
        inside, not what you've spent years mastering.</p></div>
    </div>

    <h2>How we work with companies</h2>
    <div class="ways">
      <div class="way"><span class="tag">Bulk</span>
        <h3>Bulk board orders</h3>
        <p>Lightning boards in quantity for your own builds — bare boards or
        pre-wired kits, ready for your bench or production line.</p></div>
      <div class="way"><span class="tag">OEM</span>
        <h3>OEM integration</h3>
        <p>Put Lightning inside your own product. We work with your team on
        fit, firmware and branding.</p></div>
      <div class="way"><span class="tag">Resell</span>
        <h3>Reseller &amp; distribution</h3>
        <p>Carry ZeroStick 8K products in your store, catalog or region.</p></div>
    </div>
    <div class="cta-row">
      <a href="#BizInquiry" class="button">Start a business inquiry</a>
    </div>

    {% comment %}
      The inquiry form. Shopify's built-in contact form: every field named
      contact[...] is emailed to the store inbox, so no app or backend is
      needed. Only the email field is required by Shopify.
    {% endcomment %}
    <div class="biz" id="BizInquiry">
      <h2>Business inquiries</h2>
      <p class="biz-lead">Tell us who you are, what you're building, and the
      volumes you have in mind — we answer every serious inquiry.</p>

      {%- form 'contact', id: 'BizInquiryForm', class: 'isolate' -%}
        {%- if form.posted_successfully? -%}
          <h3 class="form-status form-status-list form__message" tabindex="-1" autofocus>
            {{- 'icon-success.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
            Thanks — your inquiry is in. We'll get back to you by email.
          </h3>
        {%- elsif form.errors -%}
          <div class="form__message">
            <h3 class="form-status caption-large text-body" role="alert" tabindex="-1" autofocus>
              {{- 'icon-error.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
              Please fix the highlighted field and send again.
            </h3>
          </div>
          <ul class="form-status-list caption-large" role="list">
            <li>
              <a href="#BizInquiry-email" class="link">
                {{ form.errors.translated_fields.email | capitalize }}
                {{ form.errors.messages.email }}
              </a>
            </li>
          </ul>
        {%- endif -%}

        <div class="bizgrid">
          <div class="field">
            <input class="field__input" type="text" id="BizInquiry-company"
                   name="contact[Company]" autocomplete="organization"
                   placeholder="Company">
            <label class="field__label" for="BizInquiry-company">Company</label>
          </div>
          <div class="field">
            <input class="field__input" type="text" id="BizInquiry-name"
                   name="contact[Name]" autocomplete="name"
                   value="{% if form.name %}{{ form.name }}{% elsif customer %}{{ customer.name }}{% endif %}"
                   placeholder="Your name">
            <label class="field__label" for="BizInquiry-name">Your name</label>
          </div>
          <div class="field field--with-error">
            <input class="field__input" type="email" id="BizInquiry-email"
                   name="contact[email]" autocomplete="email" spellcheck="false"
                   autocapitalize="off" aria-required="true" required
                   value="{% if form.email %}{{ form.email }}{% elsif customer %}{{ customer.email }}{% endif %}"
                   {% if form.errors contains 'email' %}
                     aria-invalid="true" aria-describedby="BizInquiry-email-error"
                   {% endif %}
                   placeholder="Work email">
            <label class="field__label" for="BizInquiry-email">Work email
              <span aria-hidden="true">*</span></label>
            {%- if form.errors contains 'email' -%}
              <small class="contact__field-error" id="BizInquiry-email-error">
                <span class="visually-hidden">Error</span>
                <span class="form__message">
                  <span class="svg-wrapper">
                    {{- 'icon-error.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
                  </span>
                  {{- form.errors.translated_fields.email | capitalize }}
                  {{ form.errors.messages.email -}}
                </span>
              </small>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
          <div class="field">
            <input class="field__input" type="tel" id="BizInquiry-phone"
                   name="contact[Phone]" autocomplete="tel"
                   placeholder="Phone (optional)">
            <label class="field__label" for="BizInquiry-phone">Phone (optional)</label>
          </div>
          <div class="field field--select">
            <select class="field__input" id="BizInquiry-interest"
                    name="contact[Interested in]">
              <option value="Bulk board order">Bulk board order</option>
              <option value="OEM / build Lightning into our product">OEM — build Lightning into our product</option>
              <option value="Reseller / distribution">Reseller / distribution</option>
              <option value="Something else">Something else</option>
            </select>
            <label class="field__label" for="BizInquiry-interest">Interested in</label>
          </div>
          <div class="field">
            <input class="field__input" type="text" id="BizInquiry-qty"
                   name="contact[Estimated quantity]"
                   placeholder="Estimated quantity">
            <label class="field__label" for="BizInquiry-qty">Estimated quantity</label>
          </div>
          <div class="field span2">
            <textarea rows="8" id="BizInquiry-body"
                      class="text-area field__input"
                      name="contact[Message]"
                      placeholder="Tell us about your project">{{- form.body -}}</textarea>
            <label class="form__label field__label" for="BizInquiry-body">
              Tell us about your project</label>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="cta-row">
          <button type="submit" class="button">Send inquiry</button>
        </div>
      {%- endform -%}

      <p class="biz-direct">Prefer direct?
        Email <a href="mailto:reliabletrendenterprises@gmail.com">reliabletrendenterprises@gmail.com</a>
        or text <a href="tel:+13236804706">(323) 680-4706</a>.</p>
    </div>

    {% comment %}
      The ZS8K Configurator block (id="app" — the controller's setup
      drive links straight here). The two links come from the section
      settings, and the markup falls back to the GitHub defaults whenever
      a setting is blank: a page that already exists does not reliably
      pick up new schema defaults. The Windows note shows unless the
      setting is explicitly switched off (a missing value counts as on).
    {% endcomment %}
    {%- liquid
      assign zs_app_url = section.settings.app_download_url | strip
      if zs_app_url == blank
        assign zs_app_url = 'https://github.com/rtecaleb/zs8k-updates/releases/latest/download/ZS8K-Configurator.exe'
      endif
      assign zs_releases_url = section.settings.app_releases_url | strip
      if zs_releases_url == blank
        assign zs_releases_url = 'https://github.com/rtecaleb/zs8k-updates/releases'
      endif
    -%}
    <div class="app" id="app">
      <h2>Get the ZS8K Configurator</h2>
      <p class="app-lead">The free app for ZeroStick 8K controllers, for
      Windows 10 and 11: remap buttons, tune sticks and triggers, test your
      8K rate and keep the controller up to date. You don't need it to
      play — it's only for settings and updates.</p>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a href="{{ zs_app_url | escape }}" class="button">Download for Windows</a>
        <p class="app-meta">Free · Windows 10 &amp; 11 ·
          <a href="{{ zs_releases_url | escape }}" class="link" target="_blank"
             rel="noopener" aria-describedby="a11y-new-window-message">All
             versions and release notes</a></p>
      </div>

      {%- unless section.settings.show_windows_note == false %}
        <p class="app-note"><strong>Heads-up for the first launch:</strong>
        Windows may show “Windows protected your PC” the first time — click
        <strong>More info</strong>, then <strong>Run anyway</strong>. That's
        Microsoft Defender SmartScreen being careful with a new app that
        isn't code-signed yet — it isn't a virus warning. Only do this for
        the file you downloaded from this page.</p>
      {%- endunless %}

      <h3 class="app-h">Up and running in three steps</h3>
      <div class="ways app-steps">
        <div class="way"><span class="tag">Step 1</span>
          <h4>Plug in the controller</h4>
          <p>Connect it to your PC with a USB cable. It works as an
          8,000&nbsp;Hz controller straight away.</p></div>
        <div class="way"><span class="tag">Step 2</span>
          <h4>Open the ZS8K SETUP drive</h4>
          <p>A small drive called ZS8K SETUP appears in File Explorer.
          Double-click “Get the ZS8K app” to land back here — or just use
          the download button above.</p></div>
        <div class="way"><span class="tag">Step 3</span>
          <h4>Open the app</h4>
          <p>Run the file you downloaded. One click installs it, and it
          finds your controller by itself.</p></div>
      </div>

      <h3 class="app-h">What the app does</h3>
      <div class="strip app-feats">
        <div class="feat"><div class="ico">🕹️</div><h4>Buttons &amp; paddles</h4>
          <p>Remap any button and choose what each back paddle does.</p></div>
        <div class="feat"><div class="ico">🎚️</div><h4>Sticks &amp; triggers</h4>
          <p>Dead zones, response curves and hair triggers, tuned to your
          hands.</p></div>
        <div class="feat"><div class="ico">💡</div><h4>Lightbar colour</h4>
          <p>Pick any colour — the controller remembers it.</p></div>
        <div class="feat"><div class="ico">🔀</div><h4>Output modes</h4>
          <p>The native 8K PC mode, or an Xbox 360 mode for PC games that
          only understand Xbox controllers — still at 8,000&nbsp;Hz.</p></div>
        <div class="feat"><div class="ico">📈</div><h4>Live 8K rate test</h4>
          <p>Watch, second by second, how many reports your PC really
          receives.</p></div>
        <div class="feat"><div class="ico">🔄</div><h4>Controller updates</h4>
          <p>New controller firmware in one click — about 3 seconds.</p></div>
      </div>

      <h3 class="app-h">Always up to date — safely</h3>
      <div class="ways app-duo">
        <div class="way"><span class="tag">Automatic</span>
          <h4>The app updates itself</h4>
          <p>It checks for a new version when it opens and once a day,
          downloads it quietly, and switches over the next time you start
          it — or when you click <strong>Restart to update</strong>. It never
          restarts by itself, so never in the middle of a game.</p></div>
        <div class="way"><span class="tag">One click</span>
          <h4>Controller updates in about 3 seconds</h4>
          <p>When new firmware is out, the app says <strong>Controller
          update available</strong>. One click and it's done. Prefer
          hands-off? You can let it update the controller automatically —
          only ever while the controller isn't in use.</p></div>
        <div class="way"><span class="tag">Signed</span>
          <h4>Every update is signed</h4>
          <p>Each update is signed with a private key only ZeroStick holds,
          and the app refuses anything without a valid signature. Even if
          someone broke into our download site, they couldn't push fake
          software or firmware to you.</p></div>
        <div class="way"><span class="tag">Fail-safe</span>
          <h4>Safe if the cable comes out</h4>
          <p>The controller only runs new firmware once it's completely
          written and checked. If an update gets cut off, the controller
          waits in update mode — plug it back in and run the update
          again.</p></div>
      </div>

      <h3 class="app-h">No app? It still just works.</h3>
      <div class="app-text">
        <p><strong>You never need the app to play.</strong> Out of the box
        the controller is a normal 8,000&nbsp;Hz PC controller, with nothing
        to install. Your settings are saved on the controller itself, so
        they come with it to any PC.</p>
        <p><strong>The setup drive.</strong> When you plug the controller
        in, it also shows a small read-only drive called ZS8K SETUP, with a
        shortcut to this page and a short read-me. It comes back at every
        plug-in until the app has connected once — and if you never want
        the app, it stops by itself after 5 plug-ins.</p>
        <p><strong>Want the drive back later?</strong> Hold the PS button
        while you plug the controller in: it starts in PC mode for that
        session and shows the ZS8K SETUP drive again. Or click
        <strong>Show the setup drive again next plug-in</strong> on the
        app's Advanced tab.</p>
      </div>

      <h3 class="app-h">App questions</h3>
      <details><summary>Where are my settings saved?</summary>
        <p>On the controller itself. Button maps, stick and trigger tuning,
        the lightbar colour and the output mode all live in the controller,
        so they work on any PC — with or without the app.</p></details>
      <details><summary>A game doesn't see my controller. What now?</summary>
        <p>Open the app and set the output mode to Xbox 360 (Advanced tab →
        Output Mode). Almost every PC game understands an Xbox 360
        controller with no extra software, and the controller still runs at
        8,000&nbsp;Hz.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Will the app ever update my controller without asking?</summary>
        <p>Only if you turn on <strong>Update my controller
        automatically</strong> — it's off until you do. Even then it only
        updates right after you connect, while the controller isn't in
        use.</p></details>
    </div>

    <h2>Questions companies ask us</h2>
    <details><summary>What exactly can we buy?</summary>
      <p>The Lightning board itself (ZS-LTN-01) in quantity — bare boards or
      pre-wired kits — plus OEM work if you want it designed into your own
      product, and reseller terms for finished ZeroStick 8K controllers.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Do you have order minimums?</summary>
      <p>No hard minimum to start the conversation. Tell us the volumes you
      have in mind and we'll quote around them — pricing and lead times are
      quoted per inquiry.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Does it work on console?</summary>
      <p><strong>No. Lightning is a PC-only board.</strong> It does not
      connect to a PS5, Xbox or Switch — consoles cap how fast any controller
      may report, and an 8K board inside a capped console would be a fast
      engine behind a closed gate. We would rather say that plainly than sell
      you boards for the wrong machine. Building for console players? Ask us
      about the <a href="/pages/zerostick-exo">ZeroStick EXO</a> line instead.</p></details>
    <details><summary>I'm a gamer, not a company — can I still get one?</summary>
      <p>Yes — finished 8K controllers built on Lightning are coming to the
      store. The fastest way to hear the moment they're live is the
      <a href="/pages/contact">contact page</a>.</p></details>

